# Signed release build — request file

Editing this file is how a signed release build is asked for while
`.github/workflows/sign-release.yml` is not yet on the default branch (GitHub only
offers a manual-only workflow's "Run workflow" button once the file is on `main`).
It is the workflow's only push trigger, so nothing else can spend a signing run.

How to ask again: change the request line below (any change), commit and push. The run
is "build + sign + verify", it never creates a tag or a release, and its result is the
artifact `mushrea-code-signed-release` containing both signed APKs and the signer
certificate SHA-256.

The four repository secrets it needs are set once, from the keystore:
  RELEASE_KEYSTORE_BASE64 · RELEASE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD · RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS · RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD
See docs/RELEASE.md → "Signing in CI without publishing".

